        <footnote id="F1">Reflects the settlement of the restricted stock unit (&quot;RSU&quot;) awards or performance stock units (&quot;PSU&quot;) awards, as applicable, referred to in clauses (ii), (iii) and (v) of footnotes 2 and 3 below.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">In connection with the transactions contemplated by the Agreement and Plan of Merger, dated as of August 2, 2026, by and among the issuer, Armstrong Parent, Inc., and Armstrong Bidco, Inc. (the &quot;Merger Agreement&quot;), (i) each share of common stock of the issuer, par value $0.001 per share (&quot;Issuer Common Stock&quot;), held by the reporting person was converted into the right to receive $127 in cash, without interest (the &quot;Merger Consideration&quot;), (ii) each vested RSU award held by the reporting person was settled in Issuer Common Stock and subsequently converted into the right to receive the Merger Consideration, (iii) 50% of each unvested RSU award held by the reporting person (assessed on a tranche-by-tranche basis) was vested and settled in Issuer Common Stock and subsequently converted into the right to receive the Merger Agreement,...</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">(continuation of footnote 2 above). (iv) 50% of each unvested RSU award held by the reporting person (assessed on a tranche-by-tranche basis) was canceled and converted into a cash amount equal to (x) the number of shares of Issuer Common Stock subject to such RSU award, multiplied by (y) the Merger Consideration, which will be paid subject to satisfaction of the same vesting conditions that applied to the corresponding RSU award, (v) 50% of each unvested PSU award held by the reporting person (assessed on a tranche-by-tranche basis) was vested based on the greater of target performance and actual performance, settled in Issuer Common Stock and subsequently converted into the right to receive the Merger Agreement and...</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">(continuation of footnote 3 above). (vi) 50% of each unvested PSU award held by the reporting person (assessed on a tranche-by-tranche basis) was canceled and converted into a cash amount equal to (x) the number of shares of Issuer Common Stock subject to such PSU award based on the greater of target performance and actual performance, multiplied by (y) the Merger Consideration, which will be paid subject to satisfaction of the same service vesting conditions (without regard to any performance conditions) that applied to the corresponding PSU award.</footnote>
